---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import Container from '@/components/layout/Container.astro';

// NOTE: the employer non-affiliation paragraph is drafted with standard
// language. Michael reviews the exact MGB wording before launch (it is his
// name on it) — flagged in the Claude-drafted-copy review TODO.
const description =
  'Level One Radiology is educational material for clinicians. It is not medical advice, and reading it creates no physician-patient relationship.';
---

<Layout title="Disclaimer | Level One Radiology" description={description}>
  <section class="page">
    <Container width="reading">
      <header class="page-header">
        <p class="type-ui">Disclaimer</p>
        <h1 class="page-header__title">Medical Disclaimer</h1>
      </header>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="lead">
          Everything on this site is educational. None of it is medical advice.
        </p>

        <h2>Who this is for</h2>
        <p>
          This site is written for radiologists, trainees, and other clinicians. It teaches how to
          interpret emergency imaging in general. It does not, and cannot, address the care of any
          specific patient.
        </p>

        <h2>Not medical advice</h2>
        <p>
          Reading this site, subscribing to the newsletter, or emailing me does not create a
          physician-patient relationship. Nothing here is a substitute for the judgment of a
          clinician who has the whole picture: the patient, the history, the labs, and the complete
          imaging study. Diagnostic and treatment decisions belong to the treating team. If you are
          a patient looking for answers about your own imaging, talk to your physicians. They know
          your case. I do not.
        </p>

        <h2>About the cases</h2>
        <p>
          Imaging cases on this site are de-identified teaching material, prepared and reviewed
          before publication. Images may be cropped, windowed, or annotated to make a teaching point.
          The discussion around a case is teaching, not a diagnostic report, and it deliberately
          emphasizes some findings over others.
        </p>

        <h2>Accuracy</h2>
        <p>
          I work to make everything here correct at the time it is published. Medicine moves, and
          evidence, guidelines, and practice change. Older articles may not reflect current
          standards, and despite care, errors are possible. If you find one, I want to know:
          <a href="mailto:privacy@leveloneradiology.com">email me</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Independence</h2>
        <p>
          This site is written and edited by me alone. The views expressed are mine and do not
          represent the views, positions, or policies of Mass General Brigham or any other
          institution I am affiliated with. No sponsor, advertiser, or employer reviews or approves
          this content.
        </p>

        <p><em>Last updated August 8, 2026.</em></p>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>
</Layout>
